description:
FILED s543m (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27), from the reviewing session's review of s543m (F6).  PRE-EXISTING: base 9a3ce86f the same.  `docs/not-supported.md` ns-escaping-filehandle did NOT say it before s543m's records; it does now ("a holder OVERWRITTEN BY ANOTHER VALUE than a literal undef").

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl; scratch/s543m/p11/rows.pl prog 6):
    my $f = "/tmp/x.$$"; my $g = "/tmp/y.$$"; sub mk { open my $t, ">", $_[0] or die; print $t "hdata"; $t } sub sz { my $s = -s $_[0]; $s // "none" }
    my $self = { fh => mk($f) }; $self->{fh} = mk($g); print "a ", sz($f), "\n";
    my $fh = mk($f); $fh = mk($g); print "b ", sz($f), "\n";
    my %h = (fh => mk($f)); $h{fh} = 0; print "c ", sz($f), "\n";
    unlink $f, $g;
perl: a 5 / b 5 / c 5.  PCL (base and tree): a 0 / b 0 / c 0.

SAME PLACE? NO, and the COST decides the design: the drop flush is emitted only at statements that statically drop (a literal undef / `()` right side, `undef`, a void pop / shift / splice / delete; ir-spec 6.5b, s543m's measurement of #5354: `$h{k} = EXPR` is everywhere).  An overwrite by an arbitrary value would put the peek on EVERY scalar / element store, or need a type fact that the stored-over value may be a handle (VarAnnotator's `fh` facts know a lexical that held an `open`; an element does not).  Direction to measure first: the stores whose OLD value the annotator proves may be a handle (a lexical that was the target of `open my $fh` or assigned from one), counted over the corpus and the wide list, timed in a loop; everything else stays the moment of ns-escaping-filehandle.
